{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7KjzPRYE4XL5LhHepSB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote it as keeping you at two attorneys, not adding a third. With the June departure and no plan to replace her, the new hire brings you back to two. If the summary says \"third attorney,\" reviewers will see the June departure in the same paragraph, and that would hurt you more than describing the grant accurately. The accurate version still makes a strong case: without this grant, the number of tenants you can represent drops by about half.\n\n<final_document>\n**Tenant Defense Project: Keeping Eviction Defense Available in [County]**\n\nLast year, 1,140 eviction cases were filed in [County]. The Tenant Defense Project, a two-attorney legal aid clinic, represented the tenant in 163 of them. In 58% of those cases, the tenant stayed in the home or got at least 60 days to move. We turned away about 300 more tenants because no attorney was free.\n\nOur capacity is about to fall by half. Each of our attorneys carries about 80 open cases, and one leaves in June. Our last attorney search took five months, so we need to begin recruiting as soon as funding is certain.\n\nWe request $90,000 over two years ($45,000 per year) toward a staff attorney position that costs $78,000 a year with benefits. A family fund has pledged $20,000 a year for both years. The clinic will cover the remaining $13,000 a year from its general budget. With this grant, we can hire promptly and keep two full-time eviction defense attorneys rather than one.\n\nWe will measure results the same way we do now. Every six months, we will report to the Foundation the number of cases opened and how each one ended. Starting in January, we will request court-wide eviction outcome data from the [County] Clerk. We currently have no figure for how tenants without a lawyer fare. With that data, by the end of the first grant year we can compare outcomes for represented and unrepresented tenants and report the difference to the Foundation.\n\nEven at full strength, two attorneys cannot meet the need: last year we turned away 300 tenants. Without this grant, the number of tenants we can represent will fall by half.\n</final_document>\n\nIt's about 280 words. Some notes before you submit:\n\n- **\"Third attorney\":** If you actually plan to replace the departing attorney some other way, tell me and I'll change the summary back. Don't call it a third attorney unless that's true.\n- **The training month probably won't work.** The foundation decides in May, she leaves in June, and your last search took five months. That's why I left the training overlap out of the summary. If you mention it elsewhere, either start recruiting before the decision or describe a different handover, like written case files and a transition memo.\n- **County contract:** I left it out because 300 words isn't enough room to explain it well. Reviewers will likely ask about it, though. Address it in the budget or sustainability section, including what happens to your $13,000 share if the county doesn't renew.\n- **The 58%:** The summary presents it only as your own result and doesn't compare it to anything, since you have no comparison number. The clerk data plan covers that gap.\n- Fill in **[County]**, and check whether the foundation wants your name and title on the summary page."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":991,"cache_read_input_tokens":10190,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":991},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"48f96ee9-8d90-4566-a1e9-383e898013b2","uuid":"32c37eda-0e1c-4afe-b93d-8747ef9d8391","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:34:18.5